3 TOP 5 DEEP DIVES
#1 x402search-mcp: closest new MONID edge. Discovery has crossed from small
curated catalogs to five-digit endpoint indexes. Privately implication:
discovery ranking itself becomes security-sensitive because a router can
silently choose who receives data/money. Smallest experiment: same task,
query 20 providers, score capability/schema/price/provenance, permit only a
fingerprinted winner. Falsifier: search quality too poor to outperform
static providers.
#2 serverless-harness code-mode MCP: moves tool invocation into
agent-written sandbox code while keeping credentials outside. This is a
stronger architectural neighbour than another JSON-RPC gateway. Experiment:
malicious sandbox code attempts to read credential while legitimate call
succeeds through egress substitution. Falsifier: policy cannot bind
substitution tightly enough to destination/effect.
#3 Vault MCP: output-side isolation is the missing complement to call-side
authorization. Experiment against benign, obvious-injection,
encoded-injection and false-positive corpus; compare latency/TPR/FPR with
QP. Falsifier: LLM judge cost/latency dominates or adaptive attacks
trivially bypass.
#4 Kinocut: video-agent tooling is becoming typed and auditable, not just
generative. Receipts/preflight gates make it ideal for the YouTube feedback
laboratory because every edit can become a causal treatment with a
reproducible manifest. Experiment: agent edits one source into 10 variants
with one controlled variable each.
#5 MCP-ITP: strongest security lesson is that a tool can attack without
ever being called. Therefore capability admission must scan
metadata/context effects at registration/discovery time, not only execution
time.

